<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salar Jung I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1829">1829</a>–<a href="/years/1883">1883</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Mir Turab Ali Khan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Salar Jung I, born Mir Turab Ali Khan, was chief minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad-sindh">Hyderabad</a> State from 1853 until his death in 1883. He reorganised revenue collection, created modern district administration, courts, police and schools, and restored the state's finances. He kept Hyderabad loyal to the British during the rebellion of 1857 and acted as regent during the minority of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahbub-ali-khan">Mahbub Ali Khan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/salar-jung-i.jpg" alt="Salar Jung I" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: undated photo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_Salar_Jung.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
